# L1 / B002 — hooks (static analysis; hooks were not executed).

C R43 OL DEP-025 | MUST NOT (PreToolUse hook: asks the user) | Do not use npm --force or --legacy-peer-deps merely to bypass incompatible peer dependencies; resolve the actual compatibility problem. The PreToolUse hook detects --force, -f, --legacy-peer-deps (and npm config set force/legacy-peer-deps) on npm/pnpm/yarn install-like commands and asks the user to confirm. | Bash and PowerShell package-manager commands | Proceeds when the user explicitly confirms.
C R44 OL GOV-009,GOV-021 | SHOULD (PostToolUse feedback after edits; Stop reminder once per change state) | When SPECIFICATION.md or CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md changes, keep the two consistent and run the custom-settings workflow to synchronize affected code, validation, configuration, tests, documentation and frontend. | edits of product sources | Stop reminder only in a Git working tree and once per material state.
C R45 OL TST-009,TST-010 | SHOULD (Stop hook reminder: blocks stopping once per change state) | When backend production C# files changed without any backend test change, confirm existing coverage, regression tests for bug fixes and preservation of behavioral probes (verify) before finishing, or state briefly why it does not apply. | Stop event in a Git working tree | Once per material state; outside Git only an advisory system message; a continuation caused by the hook is not re-blocked.
C X10 EX DEP-001,DEP-003 | MUST (PreToolUse hook: first attempt denied) | Dependency-removal commands (npm/pnpm uninstall, remove, rm, un, unlink; yarn remove; dotnet remove package; dotnet package remove; dotnet tool uninstall; Uninstall-Package) are treated as dependency changes: the hook denies them once and routes them to the add-dependency workflow. | Bash and PowerShell commands | The identical command passes when retried within 30 minutes. | DEP-001..DEP-005 govern additions and updates; no oracle policy routes dependency removals through a workflow gate. | 'npm uninstall lodash' requested by the user is denied on first attempt; the agent must go through add-dependency and re-run the command.
C X11 EX ARC-020,ARC-001,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved; PreToolUse hook asks on every reference command; manifest hook reports removed or moved project files) | Changing the project reference graph is Reserved unless it implements the approved layout: every dotnet add/remove reference and dotnet reference add/remove command requires user confirmation, and removing or moving a .csproj is reported as a Reserved change of the project set/reference graph. | .NET project references and project files | Changes implementing the approved layout (project-structure) are not Reserved, but the hook asks anyway because it cannot tell; direct .csproj edits are only checked afterwards by the architecture check. | ARC-020 requires approval for new layers/projects and ARC-001 constrains direction; no oracle policy makes individual reference edges between existing projects (including direction-legal edges outside the documented layout) Reserved, nor requires confirmation of each reference command. | A direction-legal Api -> Domain reference needs approval, and even standard layout reference commands stop for user confirmation.

